<title>USA: Harveys Casino Q2 shr increases.</title>
<headline>Harveys Casino Q2 shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>LAKE TAHOE, Nev. 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>(dollars in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				 5/31/97   5/31/96  5/31/97   5/31/96</p>
<p> Net revenues		 $71,709  $59,380 $129,824  $108,854</p>
<p>Net income excluding</p>
<p>   nonrecurring items(a)    3,978    3,460    3,982     5,102</p>
<p> Nonrecurring items (a)	  --   ( 457)	 --  ( 2,674)</p>
<p> Net income		     3,978    3,003    3,982     2,428</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>excluding nonrecurring items</p>
<p>				     0.40     0.36     0.41	0.53</p>
<p>Nonrecurring items per share (a)</p>
<p>					 --  ( 0.05)	 --   ( 0.28)</p>
<p> Net income per share	  0.40     0.31     0.41	0.25</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding (000s)	 9,830    9,623    9,829     9,538</p>
<p>NOTE - (a) Nonrecurring expenses, net of tax, for Q2 1996 include $316,000 of preopening expenses for the May opening of land-based facilities at Harveys Casino Hotel in Council Bluffs, Iowa, and $141,000 for the early retirement of debt attributable to the application of net proceeds from the company's $150 million senior subordinated note offering.</p>
<p>Nonrecurring expenses, net of tax, for the first six months of 1996 included $2,533,000 of preopening expenses for Harveys Casino Hotel in Council Bluffs, Iowa, and $141,000 for the early retirement of debt attributable to the application of net proceeds from the company's $150 million senior subordinated note offering.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
